We aim to achieve this by categorifying the following results on homology theories:

\begin{enumerate}
\item We prove that categorical homology theories are oplax homological.

\item We prove that categorical homology admits a presentation as singular categorical homology.

\item We prove a categorified Brown representability theorem.

\item We prove a categorified Dold-Thom theorem.

\item We prove a categorified Hurewicz theorem.

\item We prove a categorified Whitehead theorem.

\item We prove that categorical $R$-homology for any rig $R$ multiplicatively lifts to the higher category of
$(R,R)$-bimodule categorical spectra.

\end{enumerate}

