Any reduced homology theory $H$ maps a homotopy cofiber sequence of pointed homotopy types $A \to B \to C$ and integer $n \in \bZ $ to a long exact sequence of abelian groups:
\begin{equation}\label{eqj}
... \to H_{n +1}(A) \to H_{n +1}(B) \to H_{n +1}(C) \to H_n(A) \to H_n(B) \to H_n(C) \to H_{n-1}(A) \to ... \end{equation}
For any reduced derived homology theory $\bar{H} : \mS_* \to \mS_*$ lifting $H$ and homotopy type $X$ 
the sequence $\{\bar{H}(X \wedge S^n)\}_{n \geq 0}$ forms a spectrum whose $n$-th bonding equivalence is
$$ \bar{H}(X \wedge S^{n}) \simeq \Omega(\bar{H}(\Sigma(X \wedge S^{n}))) = \Omega(\bar{H}(X \wedge S^{n+1})).$$
This guarantees that the derived homology theory $\bar{H}: \mS_* \to \mS_*$ lifts to a functor $\bar{H}: \mS_* \to \Sp$ to the $\infty$-category of spectra.
The sequence \ref{eqj} arises by applying homotopy groups from an exact sequence of spectra
$$... \to\bar{H}(A)[1] \to\bar{H}(B)[1] \to\bar{H}(C)[1] \to\bar{H}(A) \to\bar{H}(B) \to\bar{H}(C) \to\bar{H}(A)[-1] \to .... $$

We prove an analogue for categorical homology theories, which we call oplax homological,
for which we categorify the concept of exact sequence of spectra:
we say that an oplax left pushout square 
\begin{equation}\label{oooo}
\begin{tikzcd}
A \ar{r}{} \ar{d}[swap]{} & B \ar{d}{} \\
0 \ar{r}[swap]{} & C
\end{tikzcd}
\end{equation}
of $\infty$-categories with distinguished object or categorical spectra exhibits $C$ as the oplax left cofiber of $A \to B,$
and an oplax left pushout square 
\begin{equation}\label{oooo}
\begin{tikzcd}
A \ar{r}{} \ar{d}[swap]{} & 0 \ar{d}{} \\
B \ar{r}[swap]{} & C
\end{tikzcd}
\end{equation} exhibits $C$ as the oplax right cofiber of $A \to B.$
Dually, we define oplax left and right fibers.
We say that a sequence of $\infty$-categories with distinguished object or spectra of
$\infty$-categories
$$... \xrightarrow{\gamma_{n-1}} A_n \xrightarrow{\alpha_n} B_n \xrightarrow{\beta_n} C_n \xrightarrow{\gamma_n} A_{n+1} \xrightarrow{\alpha_{n+1}} B_{n+1}  \xrightarrow{\beta_{n+1}}  ... $$ is oplax exact if 
\begin{itemize}
\item for every even $n \in \bZ$ the morphism $\beta_n $ is the oplax left cofiber of $\alpha_n$ and fiber of $\gamma_n$,
\item for every even $n \in \bZ$ the morphism $ \gamma_n$ is the cofiber of $ \beta_n$ and oplax left fiber of $ \alpha_{n+1}$,
\item for every odd $n \in \bZ$ the morphism $\beta_n $ is the oplax right cofiber of $\alpha_n$ and fiber of $\gamma_n$,
\item for every odd $n \in \bZ$ the morphism $ \gamma_n$ is the cofiber of $ \beta_n$ and oplax right fiber of $ \alpha_{n+1}.$
\end{itemize}

\begin{theorem}\label{1}(\cref{homologic})
For every oplax cofiber sequence $A \to B \to C$ of $\infty$-categories with distinguished object and integer $n \in \bZ $ there is an induced oplax exact sequence of categorical spectra
$$... \to \bar{H}(A)[1] \to \bar{H}(B)[1] \to \bar{H}(C)[1] \to \bar{H}(A) \to \bar{H}(B) \to \bar{H}(C) \to \bar{H}(A)[-1] \to .... $$

\end{theorem}

Although of theoretical interest, \cref{1} is as useful as the notion of oplax exact sequence. 
To demonstrate the usefulness of the concept of oplax exact sequence and make categorical homology theories amenable to computations, we prove the following theorem:

\begin{theorem} \label{2}(\cref{homolog})
Consider the following commutative diagram of categorical spectra whose top and bottom sequences are oplax exact:

$$	
\begin{tikzcd}
 ... \ar{r}{\gamma_{n-1}} & A_n \ar{r}{\alpha_n} \ar{d}{\psi_n^A} & B_n \ar{d}{\psi^B_n} \ar{r}{\beta_n} & C_n \ar{d}{\psi^C_n}  \ar{r}{\gamma_n} & A_{n+1} \ar{d}{\psi^A_{n+1}} \ar{r}{\alpha_{n+1}} & B_{n+1} \ar{d}{\psi^B_{n+1}} \ar{r}{\beta_{n+1}} & ... \\ 
... \ar{r}{\gamma'_{n-1}} & A'_n \ar{r}{\alpha'_n} & B'_n \ar{r}{\beta'_n} & C'_n \ar{r}{\gamma'_n} & A'_{n+1} \ar{r}{\alpha'_{n+1}} & B'_{n+1} \ar{r}{\beta'_{n+1}} & ...
\end{tikzcd}
$$	
If any two of $\psi^A_*, \psi^B_*, \psi^C_*$ are equivalences, then so is the third.

\end{theorem}

