We prove the following Whitehead theorem for $\infty$-categories with adjoints:
\begin{theorem}(\cref{maf}) Let $\mC$ be an $(\infty, \infty)$-category with left (right) adjoints.
A functor $ \mC \to \mD$ is an equivalence if and only if the induced $\bZ$-graded functor $\Pi_*(\mC) \to \Pi_*(\mD)$ is an equivalence.

\end{theorem}
