We obtain the following Whitehead theorem for spectra of $\infty$-categories with left adjoints:

\begin{corollary}(\cref{maf}) Let $\mC$ be a spectrum of $\infty$-categories with left adjoints. % (for morphisms of arbitrary dimension).
A map $ \mC \to \mD$ of categorical spectra is an equivalence if and only if the induced $\bZ$-graded functor $\Pi_*(\mC) \to \Pi_*(\mD)$ is an equivalence.

\end{corollary}

Mimicing the definition of coefficients of a homology theory we define the coefficients of an categorical homology theory $H: \infty\Cat_* \to \infty\Cat_*$ as the $\bZ$-graded symmetric monoidal category $H_*:= \Pi_*(H(S^0)).$
We obtain the following corollary:

\begin{corollary}

Let $H, H': \infty\Cat_* \to \infty\Cat_* $
be categorical homology theories such that the coefficient categorical spectrum of $H$ admits left adjoints, and $\alpha: H \to H'$ a natural transformation.
Then $\alpha$ is an equivalence if and only if
the induced $\bZ$-graded functor on coefficients
$$ H_* \to H'_*$$
is an equivalence.

\end{corollary}

