\begin{remark}\label{lao}

If $\mC$ is an $n$-category and $\mD$ an $\m$-category for $n,\m \geq 0$,
then $\mC \boxtimes \mD$ is an $n+\m$-category.
This holds since $n\Cat$ is closed under small colimits in $\infty\Cat$ and $n\Cat$ is generated under small colimits by the lax $\ell$-cubes for $1 \leq \ell \leq n$. % by \cref{dense}.
\end{remark}

The following is \cite[Remark 3.12.7.]{GepnerHeine}:

\begin{remark}\label{grayspace}

The full subcategory $\mS \subset \infty\Cat$ is closed under the Gray tensor product and the restricted Gray monoidal structure on $\mS$ is the cartesian structure.
The left adjoint $\tau_0: \infty\Cat \to \mS$ of the resulting monoidal embedding $\mS \subset \infty\Cat$ is monoidal.

\end{remark}

