Next we consider a variant of the Gray tensor product for $\infty$-categories with distinguished object that plays the role of the smash product in homotopy theory.

\begin{definition}

The Gray smash monoidal structure on $\infty\Cat_{*}$,
denoted by $\wedge$, is the smash monoidal structure of \cite[Lemma 3.69.]{GepnerHeine}
applied to $(\infty\Cat, \boxtimes).$
For every $X, Y \in \infty\Cat_*$ the Gray smash product $X \wedge Y$ is the cofiber of the functor $X \vee Y \to X \boxtimes Y$
induced by the commutative square in $\infty\Cat:$
$$\begin{xy}
\xymatrix{
\bD^0 \boxtimes \bD^0 \ar[d] \ar[r]
& X \boxtimes \bD^0 \ar[d]
\\ 
\bD^0 \boxtimes Y \ar[r] & X \boxtimes Y.
}
\end{xy}$$

\end{definition}

\begin{notation}
Let $\mC,\mD \in \infty\Cat_*.$
Let $$ \Fun_*^{(\op)\lax}(\mC,\mD) $$ be the fiber of the functor $ \Fun^{(\op)\lax}(\mC,\mD) \to  \Fun^{(\op)\lax}(\ast,\mD)\simeq \mD$ over the base point.

\end{notation}

\cite[Lemma 2.6.11.]{GepnerHeine} gives the following:

\begin{lemma}
The Gray smash monoidal structure on $\infty\Cat_*$
is biclosed. For every $\mC,\mD \in \infty\Cat_*$ the left morphism object is $ \Fun_*^\oplax(\mC,\mD)$ and the right morphism object is $ \Fun_*^\lax(\mC,\mD)$.
\end{lemma}

