For every presentably monoidal category $\mV$ there is a 2-category of $\mV$-enriched categories and $\mV$-enriched functors equipped with a forgetful functor to the 2-category $\Cat.$

\begin{definition}
Let $\mV, \mW$ be presentably monoidal categories.

\begin{enumerate}
\item A left $\mV$-enriched category (functor) is a $\mV$-enriched category (functor).
%A left $\mV$-enriched functor is a $\mV$-enriched functor.

\item A right $\mW$-enriched category (functor) is a $\mW^\rev$-enriched category (functor).
%A right $\mW$-enriched functor is a $\mW^\rev$-enriched functor.

\item A $\mV, \mW$-bienriched category is a $\mV \ot \mW^\rev $-enriched category.
A  $\mV, \mW$-enriched functor is a $\mV \ot \mW^\rev$-enriched functor.

\end{enumerate}	

\end{definition}

In \cite{heine2024bienriched} a theory of left, right and bienriched categories is developed that 
are equivalent to the notions of the previous definition \cite[Theorem 4.89.]{heine2024bienriched}.

\begin{notation}

Let $\mV, \mW$ be presentably monoidal categories.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Let $ {_\mV\Enr}$ be the 2-category of left $\mV$-enriched categories and left $\mV$-enriched functors.

\item Let $ {\Enr_\mW} $ be the 2-category of right $\mW$-enriched categories and right $\mW$-enriched functors.

\item Let $ {_\mV\Enr_\mW} $ be the 2-category of $\mV, \mW$-bienriched categories and $\mV, \mW$-enriched functors.

\end{enumerate}	

\end{notation}

