\begin{example}

The Gray monoidal structure on $\infty\Cat$ is biclosed and so endows $\infty\Cat$ as bienriched in $(\infty\Cat,\boxtimes), (\infty\Cat,\boxtimes).$ This way we see
$\infty\Cat$ as a large Gray-category, which we denote by the same name.
Every full subcategory of $\infty\Cat$ inherits the structure of a Gray-category.
The Gray smash monoidal structure on $\infty\Cat_*$ is biclosed and endows $\infty\Cat_*$ as bienriched in $(\infty\Cat_*,\wedge), (\infty\Cat_*,\wedge).$ This way we see
$\infty\Cat_*$ as a large reduced Gray-category, which we denote by the same name.

\end{example}	

