We refer to adjunctions of (weakly) (reduced) (left) (right) (pseudo-) Gray-categories as (weakly) (reduced) (left) (right) Gray-adjunctions.

\begin{remark}\label{adj}\label{adj2}

\begin{enumerate}
\item A (reduced) left (right) Gray-functor $\mC \to \mD$ admits a right adjoint if and only if it preserves left (right) tensors and the underlying functor admits a right adjoint.

