\item A (reduced) Gray-functor $\mC \to \mD$ admits a right adjoint if and only if it preserves left and right tensors and the underlying functor admits a right adjoint.

\item A (reduced) left (right) Gray-functor $\mC \to \mD$ admits a left adjoint if and only if it preserves left (right) cotensors and the underlying functor admits a left adjoint.

