%finite colimits and left and right tensors with objects of $\infty\Cat^\omega_*$ and Gray-functors preserving finite colimits and left and right tensors with objects of $\infty\Cat^\omega_*$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}\label{pres}

%The Gray-category $\Sp$ is presentable since $\infty\Cat_*$ is a presentable Gray-category, the Gray-functor $\Omega: \infty\Cat \to \infty\Cat$ admits a left adjoint, and by ... the subcategory $\boxtimes\Pr^R\boxtimes \subset \boxtimes\widehat{\Cat}$ of presentable Gray-categories and right adjoint Gray-functors admits small limits, which are preserved by the inclusion to $\boxtimes\widehat{\Cat}.$By ... there is a canonical equivalence $\boxtimes\Pr^L\boxtimes \simeq (\boxtimes\Pr^R\boxtimes)^\op,$where the left hand side is the subcategory $\boxtimes\Pr^L\boxtimes \subset \boxtimes\widehat{\Cat}$ of presentable Gray-categories and left adjoint Gray-functors, sending left to right adjoints.
By \cref{nnmt} the Gray-category $\Sp(\mC)$ is the sequential colimit in $\wedge\Pr^L\wedge$ 
of the diagram $$\mC \xrightarrow{\Sigma} \mC^\cop \xrightarrow{\Sigma} ... $$	
The functor $\Omega: \mC \to  \mC $ preserves small filtered colimits so that the left adjoint $\Sigma:  \mC \to  \mC $ preserves compact objects. 
Let $\widehat{\rS\W}(\mC)$ be the sequential colimit of the following diagram of small reduced Gray-categories:
