\begin{proof}(3) follows from (1) and (2). (1) is dual to (2): it follows by replacing $\phi$ by $\phi^\co.$
The second half of (1) is dual to the first half of (1): it follows by replacing $\phi$ by $\phi^\op.$
So it suffices to show that every spectral left Gray-functor $\phi:\mC \to \mD$ preserves oplax pullbacks.
%We first prove that every spectral right Gray-functor $\phi:\mC \to \mD$ between spectral right Gray-categories having suspensions preserves suspensions.

