By \cref{repp} and the enriched adjoint functor theorem \cite[Theorem 3.73.]{heine2024higher} the spectral left Gray-functor $\coprod^\oplax : \Sp^{\Lambda_0^2} \to \Sp$ admits a left adjoint $\alpha$
since $\prod^\oplax \circ \Sigma$ admits a left adjoint.
For every spectral right Gray-category $\mA$ that admits small right weighted colimits the left Gray-adunction $\alpha: \Sp \rightleftarrows \Sp^{\Lambda_0^2}: \coprod^\oplax$ induces an adjunction $\alpha_\mA:= \mA \ot_{\Sp} \alpha: \mA \simeq \mA \ot_{\Sp} \Sp \rightleftarrows \mA \ot_{\Sp} \Sp^{\Lambda_0^2} \simeq \mA^{\Lambda_0^2}:  \coprod^\oplax$.
For every left adjoint spectral right Gray-functor $\F: \mA \rightleftarrows \mB: \G$ between spectral right Gray-categories having small right weighted colimits % whose right adjoint we denote by $\G$, 
there is a canonical equivalence of functors $$ \alpha_\mB \circ \F \simeq \mB \ot_{\Sp} \alpha \circ \F \ot_{\Sp} \Sp \simeq  \F \ot_{\Sp} \alpha \simeq \F \ot_{\Sp} \Sp \circ \mA \ot_{\Sp} \alpha \simeq 
\F \circ \alpha_\mA$$
providing an equivalence of right adjoints $ \G \circ \coprod^\oplax \simeq \coprod^\oplax \circ \G.$
Consequently, every right adjoint spectral right Gray-functor between spectral right Gray-categories 
having small right weighted colimits preserves oplax pushouts.
So dually, every left adjoint spectral left Gray-functor between spectral left Gray-categories 
having small left weighted limits preserves lax pullbacks. 

By spectral left Gray-Yoneda-extension \cite[Theorem 4.41., Corollary 4.46.]{heine2024bienriched} every spectral left Gray-functor $\phi:\mC \to \mD$ extends to a left adjoint spectral left Gray-functor $\phi':\mC' \to \mD'$ between presentable spectral left Gray-categories, which in particular admit small left weighted limits, along the spectral left Gray-Yoneda-embeddings, which preserve left weighted limits \cite[Corollary 3.68.]{heine2024higher} and in particular lax pullbacks. Thus $\phi:\mC \to \mD$ preserves lax pullbacks.

\end{proof}

