\subsection{Oplax exact sequences}

In this subsection we categorify the concept of long exact sequence from homological algebra.
We use this categorification to formulate and prove that homology theories are homological in a categorified sense (\cref{homologic}).

\begin{proposition}\label{laxfib}
Let $\mC$ be a reduced spectral right Gray-category that admits oplax left fibers and suspensions.
Then $\mC$ admits oplax left cofibers and the canonical map $$\xi: \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \coprod}  \to \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \coprod} \circ \Sigma$$ of functors $\mC^{\bD^1} \to \mC$  is an equivalence.

%Let $\mC$ be a spectral Gray-category that admits lax cofibers and lax fibers.The canonical map $$\xi: \overset{\overset{\hspace{-0.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{0.0mm} \oplax}}{\coprod 0} \to \overset{\overset{\hspace{-0.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{0.0mm} \oplax}}{\prod} 0 \circ \Sigma$$ of spectral left Gray-functors $\mC^{\bD^1} \to \mC$  is an equivalence. %admits a left inverse.	

\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}
By \cite[Lemma 3.80., Remark 3.85.]{heine2024higher} there is a spectral right Gray-embedding of $\mC$ into a presentable spectral right Gray-category that preserves oplax left fibers and suspensions. So we can assume that $\mC$ is presentable.	
%By definition the map $\kappa: \overset{\overset{\hspace{-0.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{0.0mm} \oplax}}{\coprod} \to  \Sigma \circ (\overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod} \times_{\ev_0} \prod^\oplax 0) \circ \Sigma$ of spectral left Gray-functors $\mC^{\Lambda_0^2} \to \mC$ factors as $$ \coprod^\oplax \to \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \coprod}\times_{\Sigma \ev_0} \coprod^\oplax 0 \to \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod}\circ \Sigma \times_{\ev_0 \circ \Sigma} \prod^\oplax 0 \circ \Sigma \simeq (\overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod}\times_{\ev_0} \prod^\oplax 0) \circ \Sigma.$$
Restricting $\kappa$ along the spectral right Gray-functor $\mC^{\bD^1} \to \mC^{\Lambda_0^2}, \ Y \leftarrow X  \mapsto Y \leftarrow X \to 0$ gives $\xi$ so that $\xi$ admits a left inverse by
\cref{repp}.
%the canonical map$$ \xi: \coprod^\oplax 0 \simeq \Sigma \ev_0 \times_{\Sigma \ev_0} \coprod^\oplax 0 \to \ev_0 \circ \Sigma \times_{\ev_0 \circ \Sigma} \prod^\oplax 0 \circ \Sigma \simeq \prod^\oplax 0 \circ \Sigma.$$So in view of \cref{ttut} the map $\kappa: \coprod^\oplax \to  \Sigma \circ (\overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod} \times_{\ev_0} \prod^\oplax 0) \circ \Sigma$ of spectral left Gray-functors $\mC^{\Lambda_0^2} \to \mC$ is an equivalence if and only if$\xi$ is an equivalence.By \cref{repp} the canonical $\kappa$ and so $\xi$ admit a left inverse. 
By the adjoint functor theorem %\cite[Theorem 3.73.]{heine2024higher} 
the functor $\overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \coprod}$ admits a left adjoint since $ \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod} \circ \Sigma$ does. Replacing $\mC$ by $\mC^\op$ %which is a spectral Gray-category that admits lax pushouts, fibers and lax fibers, \cref{repp} implies that 
the functor $\overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod}$ admits a right adjoint.
Hence in the adjunction $L: \Sp \rightleftarrows \Sp^{\bD^1}: \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod}$ both adjoints admit a right adjoint so that the latter adjunction induces an adjunction $L: \mC \simeq \mC \otimes_{\Sp}\Sp \rightleftarrows \mC^{\bD^1} \simeq \mC \otimes_{\Sp}\Sp^{\bD^1}: \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod}$.
This implies that $\mC \ot_{\Sp}  \xi_\Sp: \mC \ot_{\Sp} \overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \coprod} \to \mC \ot_{\Sp} (\overset{\overset{\hspace{2.0mm}\rightarrow}{\hspace{2.0mm} \oplax}}{0 \prod} \circ \Sigma)$ %of left adjoint spectral left Gray-functors $\Sp^{\bD^1} \to \Sp $ induces under the functor $\mC \ot_{\Sp} (-)$ the respective map 
is $\xi_\mC.$ %of left adjoint spectral left Gray-functors $\mC^{\bD^1} \to \mC$.
Hence we can assume that $\mC =\Sp$. 
In this case $\xi$ is a map of spectral left Gray-functors $\Sp^{\bD^1}\to \Sp$.
Since $\Sp^{\bD^1} $ is generated under small colimits and left tensors by
