\begin{corollary}\label{domon}
Let $\mC$ be a reduced Gray-category that admits suspensions, endomorphisms and sequential colimits. Every reduced Gray-functor $\phi: \mC \to \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat)$ that preserves suspensions, endomorphisms and sequential colimits also preserves oplax pushouts.

\end{corollary}

\begin{proof}By \cref{domonos} the reduced Gray-functor $\phi_* :  \Pre\Sp(\mC) \to \Pre\Sp(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat))$ 
restricts to a reduced Gray-functor $\phi_!:  \Sp(\mC) \to \Sp(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat)) \simeq  \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\Sp) \simeq \Sp,$ where the last equivalence is by \cref{hhoo},
that preserves infinite suspension spectra.
By \cref{symsp} the infinite suspension spectrum Gray-functor of $  \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\Sp)$ is the Gray-embedding
$B^\infty:  \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\Sp) \to \Sp(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat)) \simeq  \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\Sp) \simeq \Sp, $ which as a left adjoint Gray-embedding detects oplax pushouts.
In other words there is a canonical equivalence $ \phi_! \circ \Sigma^\infty \simeq B^\infty \circ \phi.$ 
Hence $\phi$ preserves oplax pushouts because $ \phi_! \circ \Sigma^\infty$ preserves oplax pushouts as a left adjoint Gray-functor.

\end{proof}

