\begin{lemma}\label{locpre}Let $\mC$ be a small reduced right Gray-category that admits suspensions, $\mD$ a reduced right presentable Gray-category and $X \in \mC$.
The left Gray-functor $${\nu_X: \Fun\wedge}(\mC,\mD) \to \Pre\Sp(\mD)$$
preserves local equivalences.	

\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}

We prove that $\nu_X$ sends generating local equivalences to local equivalences.
Let $\kappa$ be a strongly inaccessible cardinal such that the underlying $\infty$-category of $\mD$ is $\kappa$-compactly generated. We use the notation of the proof of \cref{excloc}.
We verify that $\nu_X$ sends the generating local equivalence $(Y \wedge (-)) \circ \zeta_{Z} $ for $Z \in \mC $ and $Y \in \mD^\kappa$ to a local equivalence.
The left Gray-functor $\nu_X$ sends $(Y \wedge (-)) \circ \zeta_{Z} $ to $(Y \wedge (-)) \circ \nu_X(\zeta_{Z}) $.

The right Gray-adjunction $ Y \wedge (-) : \infty\Cat_* \rightleftarrows \mD: \R\Mor_\mD(Y,-)$ gives rise to a right Gray-adjunction $$(Y \wedge (-))_!: \Pre\Sp \rightleftarrows \Pre\Sp(\mD): \R\Mor_\mD(Y,-)_!.$$ The right adjoint of the second adjunction preserves spectra since the right adjoint of the first adjunction preserves endomorphisms. Thus the left adjoint of the
second adjunction preserves local equivalences.
%The left Gray-functor $(Y \wedge (-))_!: \Pre\Sp \to \Pre\Sp(\mD)$ preserves local equivalences since its right Gray right adjoint $(\R\Mor_\mD(Y,-))_! : \Pre\Sp(\mD) \to \Pre\Sp$ preserves spectra as the right adjoint right Gray-functor $\R\Mor_\mD(Y,-) : \mD \to \infty\Cat_*$ preserves endomorphisms.
So it suffices to show that $\nu_X$ sends $\zeta_{Z} $ to a local equivalence. The morphism $\nu_X(\zeta_{Z})$ identifies with the morphism
%$$  \Sigma(\R\Mor_{\mC}(\Sigma(Z),X \wedge S^\bullet)) \simeq$$
$$ \Sigma(\Omega( \R\Mor_{\mC}(Z,X \wedge S^\bullet))) \to \R\Mor_{\mC}(Z, X \wedge S^\bullet). $$

Let $T:= \R\Mor_{\mC}(Z, X \wedge S^\bullet)\in \Pre\Sp(\mD)$ and $L$ the left adjoint of the embedding $$\Sp(\mD) \subset \Pre\Sp(\mD).$$
We like to see that the canonical morphism $$\Sigma(L(\Omega(T))) \simeq L(\Sigma(\Omega(T))) \to L(T)$$ in $\Sp(\mC)$ 
is an equivalence.
The latter factors as  $$\Sigma(L(\Omega(T))) \to \Sigma(\Omega(L(T)))  \to L(T).$$
The first morphism is an equivalence since $L$ is a right Gray left adjoint and so preserves suspensions  and moreover preserves endomorphisms by \cref{spectri}, the second morphism is an equivalence by right stability of $\Sp(\mC)$ of \cref{rstab}.

We can also give an alternative proof. By \cref{lefffa} the reduced left Gray-functor functor $\nu_X$ admits a right adjoint $\N$. 
The left Gray-functor $\nu_X$ preserves local equivalences if and only if the right adjoint preserves local objects. So we need to see that for every $\E \in \Sp(\mD)$ the reduced right Gray-functor
$\N(\E)$ is oplax excisive or equivalently that for every $Z \in \mD$ the reduced right Gray-functor
$\R\Mor_\mD(Z,-)\circ \N(\E): \mC \to \infty\Cat_*$ is oplax excisive.
By adjointness for every $\E \in \Pre\Sp(\mD)$ and $Z \in \mD$
the reduced right Gray-functor $\R\Mor_\mD(Z,-)\circ \N(\E): \mC \to \infty\Cat_*$
factors as reduced right Gray-functors $$\mC \subset  {\Fun\wedge}(\mC,\infty\Cat_*)^\circ \xrightarrow{\nu^\circ_X} \Pre\Sp^\circ \xrightarrow{\L\Mor_{\Pre\Sp}(-,(-)^ Z_*(\E))}  \infty\Cat_*. $$
If $\E \in \Sp(\mD)$, then $(-)^Z_*(\E) \in \Sp$ and the latter composition factors as reduced right Gray-functors
 $$\mC  \subset  {\Fun\wedge}(\mC,\infty\Cat_*)^\circ \xrightarrow{\nu^\circ_X} \Pre\Sp^\circ \xrightarrow{L^\circ} \Sp^\circ \xrightarrow{\L\Mor_{\Sp}(-,(-)^Z_*(\E))}  \infty\Cat_*. $$

The opposite of the left enriched Yoneda-embedding $$ \mC \subset {\Fun\wedge}(\mC,\infty\Cat_*)^\circ$$ preserves right tensors \cite[Corollary 3.67.]{heine2024higher}. 
The reduced right Gray-functor $$\nu_X^\circ : {\Fun\wedge}(\mC, \infty\Cat_*)^\circ \to \Pre\Sp^\circ$$ preserves right tensors. By \cref{spectri} the spectrification $L: \Pre\Sp \to \Sp$ preserves double endomorphisms so that the opposite of it preserves double suspensions.
So $\N(\E)$ is oplax excisive by \cref{Homt} and \cref{coext} if $\E \in \Sp(\mD)$. 

%preserves left tensors and the local equivalences in source and target of $\nu$ are closed under left tensors, it is moreover enough to see that $ \zeta_{X,n} $ is sent by $\nu$ to a local equivalenc

\end{proof}

\begin{corollary}\label{locpre2}Let $\mC$ be a small reduced right Gray-category that admits suspensions, $\mD$ a reduced presentable Gray-category and $X \in \mC$.
