\begin{notation}
Let $\mC, \mD$ be reduced right Gray-categories. 
Let $$ {\mathrm{Fil}\Fun\wedge}(\mC,\mD) \subset {\Fun\wedge}(\mC,\mD)$$ 	
be the full subcategory of reduced right Gray-functors preserving small filtered colimits.


Let $$ {\mathrm{Fil}\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC,\mD) \subset {\Fun\wedge}(\mC,\mD)$$ 	
be the full subcategory of oplax excisive right Gray-functors preserving small filtered colimits.
\end{notation}

\begin{lemma}\label{rioko}

Let $\mD$ be a reduced pseudo-Gray-category whose underlying reduced left pseudo-Gray-category is a presentable left Gray-category.
The full subcategory $$\mH(\mD) \subset {\Fil\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD)$$
is closed under small colimits and left tensors. % and coendomorphisms.

\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}

Let $H: \infty\Cat_* \to \mD$ be a reduced and oplax excisive right Gray-functor and $X \in \infty\Cat_*.$
\cref{spectri} implies that the right tensor $H(S^\bullet) \wedge X$ in $\Sp(\mD)$ is the spectrum associated to the prespectrum $$((-)\wedge X)_! (H(S^\bullet)).$$	
The canonical map of prespectra \begin{equation}\label{ijjmn}
((-)\wedge X)_! (H(S^\bullet)) \to H(S^\bullet \wedge X) \end{equation} 
induces a map of spectra 
\begin{equation}\label{ijjm}
H(S^\bullet) \wedge X \to H(S^\bullet \wedge X) .\end{equation} 
The image under $\Omega^\infty$ of \ref{ijjm} is the functor \ref{eqzz}. Since $H$ is oplax excisive, for every$\ell \geq 0 $ the map of spectra $$ H(S^\bullet) \wedge \Sigma^\ell(X) \to H(S^\bullet \wedge \Sigma^\ell(X)) \simeq \Sigma^\ell(\Omega^\ell(H(S^\bullet \wedge \Sigma^\ell(X))))$$
identifies with the following map of spectra
$$ \Sigma^\ell(H(S^\bullet) \wedge X) \to \Sigma^\ell( H(S^\bullet \wedge X)).$$
So the functor \ref{eqzz} is an equivalence for every $X \in \infty\Cat_*$ if and only if the map of spectra \ref{ijjm} is an equivalence for every $X \in \infty\Cat_*$.
In particular, a reduced and oplax excisive right Gray-functor $H:\infty\Cat_* \to \mD$ is a lax homology theory if and only if for every $X \in \infty\Cat_*$ the map of spectra \ref{ijjm} is an equivalence.

For every $X \in \infty\Cat_* $ there is a canonical natural transformation $$\rho: ((-) \wedge X) \circ \nu \to \nu^X $$
of reduced left Gray-functors $$ {\Fun\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \to \Pre\Sp(\mD)$$ whose component at any
$H \in {\Fun\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD)$ is the morphism \ref{ijjmn}.
$ H(S^\bullet) \wedge X \to H (S^\bullet \wedge X).$
Let $\iota: {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \subset {\Fun\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD)$ be the canonical embedding.
The latter transformation gives rise to a natural transformation $$L \circ \rho \circ \iota:  ((-) \wedge X) \circ \nu  \to \nu^X $$
of functors $ {\Fil\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \to \Sp(\mD)$
whose component at any $H \in {\Fil\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) $ is the morphism \ref{ijjm}. 
In the first part of the proof we showed that $\mH(\mD) \subset {\Fil\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD)$ is the full subcategory spanned by those $H$ such that $\rho_H$ is an equivalence.
Source and target of $\rho$ preserve small colimits and left tensors.
By \cref{locpre} source and target of $L \circ \rho \circ \iota$ preserve local equivalences and therefore also preserve small colimits and left tensors. 
Consequently, the full subcategory $\mH(\mD) \subset {\Fil\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD)$
is closed under small colimits and left tensors.

\end{proof}


