Since $\mH(\mD)$ is oplax stable, %and $\mH(\mD)$ is closed in $ {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) $ and so also closed in ${\Fun\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD)$ under double endomorphisms by \cref{rioko}, %
%by \cref{lifti} 
the oplax excisive Gray-functor $\gamma: \mH(\mD) \to \mD$ preserves endomorphisms and so 
induces a Gray-functor $$\mH(\mD) \simeq \Sp(\mH(\mD)) \to \Sp(\mD)$$ that preserves endomorphisms and so is oplax excisive and lifts $\gamma$ and so by uniqueness of \cref{lifti} identifies with the Gray-functor $\bar{\gamma}.$
The underlying left Gray-functor of $\gamma$ evaluating at $S^0$ factors as left Gray-functors
$$\mH(\mD) \xrightarrow{\nu}\Sp(\mD) \xrightarrow{\Omega^\infty} \mD.$$
Consequently, the underlying left Gray-functor of $\bar{\gamma}$,
which  factors as $\mH(\mD) \simeq \Sp(\mH(\mD)) \to \Sp(\mD)$, 
factors as $$ \mH(\mD) \simeq \Sp(\mH(\mD)) \to \Sp(\Sp(\mD)) \simeq \Sp(\mD)$$ and so identifies with $\nu: \mH(\mD) \to \Sp(\mD).$
So $\bar{\gamma}$ induces the equivalence $\nu$ on underlying left Gray-categories and 
so by \cref{adj}  is an equivalence of Gray-categories if and only if it preserves right tensors.
For that we need to verify that for every $Y \in \infty\Cat_*$ and $\F \in \mH(\mD) $ the canonical morphism $$\theta: \nu(\F) \wedge Y \to \nu(\F \wedge Y)$$ is an equivalence.
Since $\F \in \mH(\mD)$, there is an $\E \in \Sp(\mD)$ such that 
$\F \simeq \Omega^\infty(\E \wedge (-))$ and $\theta$ identifies with the canonical equivalence
$$\nu(\F) \wedge Y \simeq \E \wedge Y \simeq \nu(\Omega^\infty(\E \wedge Y \wedge (-))) \simeq \nu(\Omega^\infty(\E \wedge (-)) \circ (Y\wedge(-))) \simeq  \nu(\F \wedge Y).$$ 

%The latter morphism induces at even level $n \geq 0$, i.e. after applying $\Omega^\infty \circ \Sigma^n$,the canonical equivalence:
%$$(\nu(\F) \wedge Y)_n \simeq$$$$ \colim_{\ell \geq 0} \Omega^\ell(\nu(\F)_{n+\ell} \wedge Y) 
%= $$$$ \colim_{\ell \geq 0} \Omega^\ell(\F(S^{n+\ell}) \wedge Y) \simeq $$$$\colim_{\ell \geq 0} \Omega^\ell(\F(S^{n+\ell} \wedge Y)) \simeq $$$$ \colim_{\ell \geq 0} \Omega^\ell(\F(Y \wedge S^{n+\ell})) \simeq $$$$ \colim_{\ell \geq 0} \Omega^\ell(\F(Y \wedge S^n \wedge S^{\ell})) \simeq $$$$ \colim_{\ell \geq 0} \F(Y \wedge S^n) \simeq $$$$  \F(Y\wedge S^n) = $$$$\nu(\F \circ (Y \wedge (-)))_n. $$

\vspace{1mm}

We prove next that the Gray-functor $\bar{\beta}: \Fil{\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \to \Sp(\mD)$ admits a left adjoint.
Let $$\zeta:=\bar{\gamma} \circ R: \Fil{\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \to \mH(\mD)\to \Sp(\mD)$$ be the composition of right adjoint Gray-functors.
By definition the underlying left Gray-functor of $\zeta$ is right adjoint to $\Phi$
and so identifies with $\nu.$
By definition the Gray-functor $\zeta$ factors as $$ \Fil{\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \xrightarrow{R} \mH(\mD)\subset  \Fil{\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \xrightarrow{\bar{\beta}} \Sp(\mD).$$
So the counit $\epsilon: R \to \id$ of the Gray-adjunction $\mH(\mD) \rightleftarrows \Fil{\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD):R$ yields a map of Gray-functors
$\bar{\beta} \epsilon:  \zeta \to \bar{\beta}$. 
By the triangle identities the counit $\epsilon: R \to \id$ is inverted by $R$ and so inverted by $\nu$,
and so inverted by $\bar{\beta}$ that induces $\nu$ on underlying left Gray-categories.
Hence the map $ \bar{\beta} \epsilon$ is an equivalence. So the Gray-functor $\bar{\beta}: \Fil{\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) \to \Sp(\mD)$ admits a left adjoint.

%Consequently, the underlying left Gray-functor of $\zeta$ is left adjoint to $\N.$We complete the proof by showing that $\zeta$ preserves right tensors and so admits a right adjointby \cref{adj}. Since $\zeta$ refines $\nu$, we need to verify that for every $Y \in \infty\Cat_*$ and $\F \in \Fil{\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\infty\Cat_*,\mD) $ the canonical morphism $\nu(\F) \wedge Y \to \nu(\F \wedge Y)$ is an equivalence.

\end{proof}

\begin{corollary}\label{lifta}Let $H: \infty\Cat_* \to \infty\Cat_*$ be an categorical homology theory.
There is a unique categorical homology theory  $\bar{H}: \infty\Cat_* \to \Sp$ lifting $H.$

\end{corollary}

\begin{proof}

This follows from \cref{Brown} and that $\Sp(\Sp) \simeq \Sp$ by stability of
$\Sp$ by \cref{stab}.

\end{proof}

We obtain as an immediate corollary that categorical homology theories are oplax homological.

\begin{theorem}\label{homologic} Let $H: \infty\Cat_* \to \infty\Cat_*$ be an categorical homology theory.
For every oplax cofiber sequence $A \to B \to C$ in $\infty\Cat_*$ and $n \in \bZ $ there is an induced oplax exact sequence in $\Sp$:
$$... \to \bar{H}(A)[1] \to \bar{H}(B)[1] \to \bar{H}(C)[1] \to \bar{H}(A) \to \bar{H}(B) \to \bar{H}(C) \to \bar{H}(A)[-1] \to .... $$

\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}

By \cref{Brown} there is a unique $E \in \Sp$ such that $H \simeq \Omega^\infty(E \wedge(-))$ as reduced right Gray-functors. Moreover by the uniqueness statement in \cref{Brown} there is a canonical equivalence $\bar{H} \simeq E \wedge (-) $ of reduced right Gray-functors 
$\infty\Cat_* \to \Sp.$
Hence $\bar{H}$ factors as reduced right Gray-functors $ \infty\Cat_* \xrightarrow{\Sigma^\infty} \Sp \xrightarrow{E \wedge(-)} \Sp.$
The first reduced right Gray-functor $ \Sigma^\infty: \infty\Cat_* \to \Sp $ is a left adjoint and so preserves oplax cofibers.
The second right Gray-functor $E \wedge(-): \Sp \xrightarrow{} \Sp$ preserves $\Sigma$ and so also $\Omega$ by stability. Moreover it preserves oplax exact sequences by \cref{puppe} (2). So the claim follows.

\end{proof}

