\subsection{A categorical Hurewicz theorem}

In this subsection we prove a categorified Hurewicz theorem.

\begin{definition}Let $\mC \in \infty\Cat.$
The set of weak equivalence classes of $\mC$ is $\pi_0(\iota_0(\mC))$,
the set of equivalence classes in the classifying space of $\mC.$	

\end{definition}

\begin{remark}
The set $\pi_0(\tau_0(\mC))$ is the quotient of the set of equivalence classes $\pi_0(\iota_0(\mC))$ 
of $\mC$ after the equivalence relation being connected by a zig-zag of morphisms.
\end{remark}

\begin{remark}
The canonical embedding $\Set \subset \infty\Cat$ 
admits a left adjoint that sends an $\infty$-category $\mC$ to $\pi_0(\tau_0(\mC))$,
the set of weak equivalence classes in $\mC.$	

\end{remark}

\begin{theorem}
Let $n \geq0$ and $\mC \in \infty\Cat_*$ be $n$-connected and $R$ a rig.
Then $H(\mC;R)$ is $n$-connected and the functor $\Omega^{n+1}(\mC) \to \Omega^{n+1}(H(\mC;R))$ induces on weak equivalence classes
the universal map to the free left $R$-module in $\C\mon$ (on the abelianization).

\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}

For every $n \geq 0$ let $ \infty\Cat^{\leq n} \subset \infty\Cat $ be the full subcategory of $n$-connected $\infty$-categories. 
We prove first that for every $m \geq 0$ the free functor $\infty\Cat_* \to {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat))}$ sends $n$-connected $\infty$-categories with distinguished object to left $R$-modules whose underlying $\infty$-category is $n$-connected. 
Since the full subcategory $ \infty\Cat^{\leq n} \subset \infty\Cat $ is closed under finite products,
there is an induced embedding 
$ \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat^{\leq n}) \subset \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat)$ whose essential image precisely consists of the symmetric monoidal $\infty$-categories whose underlying $\infty$-category is $n$-connected. By \cref{hujt} the full subcategory $ \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat^{\leq n}) \subset  \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat)$
is closed under the monoidal structure induced by the Gray-tensor product.
So there is an induced embedding 
$ {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat^{\leq n}))} \subset {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat))}$ whose essential image precisely consists of the $R$-modules whose underlying $\infty$-category is $n$-connected. 

By \cref{deloop} there is an adjunction
\begin{equation}\label{adki} B^{n+1}: \Mon_{\bE_{n+1}}(\infty\Cat)  \rightleftarrows \infty\Cat_*: \Omega^{n+1}\end{equation}
whose left adjoint preserves finite products and induces an equivalence to $ \infty\Cat_*^{\leq n} \subset \infty\Cat_* .$
Hence we obtain an induced adjunction
$$B^{n+1}: \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\Mon_{\bE_{n+1}}(\infty\Cat)) \simeq \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat) \rightleftarrows \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat_*) \simeq \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat): \Omega^{n+1}$$
whose left adjoint is an embedding, and which by \cref{deoo} underlies a reduced left Gray-adjunction
$B^{n+1}: \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat) \rightleftarrows  \Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat) : \Omega^{n+1}. $
Moreover the left adjoint $B^{n+1}$ is a linear left $\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat)$-enriched functor,
which tensors from the right with the free reduced $\bE_\infty$-algebra on $S^{n+1}.$
Hence the latter adjunction gives rise to an adjunction on left $R$-modules
\begin{equation}\label{adio}
B^{n+1}: {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat))} \rightleftarrows  {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat))}  : \Omega^{n+1}\end{equation}
whose left adjoint induces an equivalence to the full subcategory $ {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat^{\leq n}))}$ and which covers adjunction \ref{adki}.
Hence there is a commutative square 
of right adjoints
$$\begin{xy}
\xymatrix{
{_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat))} \ar[d] \ar[rr]^{B^{n+1} \circ \Omega^{n+1}}
&& {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat ^{\leq n}))} \ar[d]
\\ 
\infty\Cat_*  \ar[rr]^{B^{n+1} \circ \Omega^{n+1}} && \infty\Cat^{\leq n}_*.
}
\end{xy}$$	

Thus there is a commutative square of left adjoints 
$$\begin{xy}
\xymatrix{
\infty\Cat^{\leq n}_* \ar[d] \ar[rr]
&& \infty\Cat_* \ar[d]^{H(-;R)}
\\ 
{_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat^{\leq n}))}  \ar[rr] && {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat))}.
}
\end{xy}$$	

We prove the second part. By the first part for every $n$-connected $\mC \in \infty\Cat_*$
the functor $ \mC \to H(\mC;R) $
exhibits the target as free on $\mC$ in the category $_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat^{\leq n})).$
Using adjunction \ref{adio} the functor $ \Omega^{n+1}(\mC) \to \Omega^{n+1}(H(\mC;R)) $
exhibits the target as free $R$-modules in $\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat) $ on $  \Omega^{n+1}(\mC) \in \Mon_{\bE_{n+1}}(\infty\Cat) $.
The embedding $\Set \subset \mS \subset \infty\Cat$ admits a left adjoint that factors as
$ \pi_0 \circ \tau_0$ and so preserves finite products.
The adjunction $ \pi_0 \circ \tau_0: \infty\Cat \rightleftarrows \Set$ induces an adjunction
$_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\infty\Cat)) \rightleftarrows {_R\Mod(\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\Set))}$
that covers the former adjunction. Since the right adjoints agree via the forgetful functors,
the left adjoint preserves the free functors. Hence the functor 
$ \pi_0(\tau_0(\Omega^{n+1}(\mC))) \to \pi_0(\tau_0(\Omega^{n+1}(H(\mC;R)))) $
exhibits the target as free $R$-module in $\Mon_{\bE_\infty}(\Set) $ on $  \pi_0(\tau_0(\Omega^{n+1}(\mC))) \in \Mon_{\bE_{n+1}}(\Set) $.

