We obtain the following:

\begin{theorem}\label{disk1}

Let $\bk \geq 0.$ The following $\infty$-categories are equivalent:

\begin{enumerate}
\item The categorical homology of $\bD^k_+$, i. e. $ \Omega^\infty(H(\bN)\wedge \bD_+^k)$.

\item The free strict commutative monoid in $\Fun(\Theta^\op,\mS) $ generated by the nerve of $\bD^k$.

\item The free strict symmetric monoidal $\infty$-category generated by $\bD^k$.

\item The free strict symmetric monoidal strict $\infty$-category generated by $\bD^k$.

\item The coproduct $ \coprod_{n \geq0} (\bD^k)^{\vee n}$

\end{enumerate}

%In particular, the categorical homology of $\bD^1_+$ is a partially ordered set. %strict $(1,1)$-category.

\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
By 	\cref{theuta} the objects of (1) and (3) are equivalent. By 	\cref{free} the categorical homology of $\bD^n_+$ is the coproduct $ \coprod_{n \geq0} \D^n(\bD^k),$ which by definition is the localization of $ \coprod_{n \geq0} \D^n \circ \N(\bD^k),$
where $\N: \infty\Cat \to \Fun(\Theta^\op, \mS)$ is the restricted Yoneda-embedding. 
%The presheaf $\N(\bD^1)$ factors as $\Theta^\op \xrightarrow{\tau_1} \Delta^\op \xrightarrow{\Delta^1} \Set \subset \mS$, where $\tau_1$ is the restricted 1-truncation.So by \cref{helpo} and the definition of $\D^n$ the presheaf $\D^n \circ \N(\bD^1)$ factors as $\Theta^\op \to \Delta^\op \xrightarrow{\Delta^n} \Set \subset \mS$, which is $\N([n]),$ and so is local.
By \cref{coufo} the presheaf $ \coprod_{n \geq0} \D^n \circ \N(\bD^k)$ is equivalent to $ \N(\coprod_{n \geq0} (\bD^k)^{\vee n}) $ and so is local. So the localization of $ \coprod_{n \geq0} \D^n \circ \N(\bD^k) \simeq \N(\coprod_{n \geq0} (\bD^k)^{\vee n})$ is $\coprod_{n \geq0} (\bD^k)^{\vee n} $ whose image under $\N$ is $ \coprod_{n \geq0} \D^n \circ \N(\bD^k), $ which by \cref{polujk} is the free strict commutative monoid on $\N(\bD^k).$ So the objects of (1) and (5) and (2) are equivalent.
 The free strict symmetric monoidal strict $\infty$-category on $\bD^k$ is 
the localization of $ \coprod_{n \geq0} \D^n \circ \N(\bD^k)\simeq \coprod_{n \geq0} \N(\bD^k)^{\times n}_{\Sigma_n}\simeq \coprod_{n \geq0} \N((\bD^k)^{\times n})_{\Sigma_n}  \in \Fun(\Theta^\op, \Set) $
with respect to the localization $  \Fun(\Theta^\op, \Set)  \to \infty\Cat^\strict. $ 
By \cref{coufo} the presheaf $ \coprod_{n \geq0} \D^n \circ \N(\bD^k) \in \Fun(\Theta^\op, \Set) $ is $ \N(\coprod_{n \geq0} (\bD^k)^{\vee n})$ and so is local. Thus the free strict symmetric monoidal strict $\infty$-category on $\bD^k$ is $ \coprod_{n \geq0} (\bD^k)^{\vee n} $. So the objects of (4) and (5) are equivalent.

\end{proof}

