%This Eilenberg-Moore object is a morphism $\mX \to \mV $ in ${_{\mV}\Mod_\mV}(\widehat{\Cat})$ that lies over the right $\mV$-linear functor ${{_A\Mod}(\mV)}\to \mV$.
Under the canonical equivalence ${_{\mV}\Mod_\mV}(\widehat{\Cat}) \simeq {_\mV\Mod(\Mod_\mV(\widehat{\Cat}))}$ of \cite[Remark 4.83.]{heine2024bienriched} the $\mV,\mV$-bitensored category $\mX$ corresponds to a left $\mV$-action on ${_A\Mod}(\mV)$ with respect to the left 
$ \widehat{\Cat}$-action on $\Mod_\mV(\widehat{\Cat}).$ The latter corresponds to a monoidal functor $$\mV \to \Enr\Fun_\mV^L({_A\Mod}(\mV), {{_A\Mod}(\mV)}) \simeq {{_A}\Mod_A(\mV)}$$
that sends $V$ to $A \ot V \simeq V \ot A$, where the last equivalence is by \cite[Theorem 4.8.4.1.]{lurie.higheralgebra}, \cite[Remark 4.83.]{heine2024bienriched}.
\end{proof}

