\begin{remark}
Let $\mC$ be a quasi-stable Gray-category. Quasi-stability implies that $ {\wedge\Exc^\mH\wedge}(\mC, \mD) \subset {\wedge\Fun\wedge}(\mC, \mD) $ precisely consists of the reduced Gray-functors preserving endomorphisms, coendomorphisms and $\mH$-weighted limits. %Hence ${\wedge\Fun^\pi\wedge}(\mC, \mD) \subset {\wedge\Exc\wedge}(\mC, \mD).$
In particular, the Gray-Yoneda-embedding induces a Gray-embedding $$\mC \hookrightarrow {\wedge\Exc^\mH \wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*\boxplus \infty\Cat_*)$$ 
