\begin{theorem}\label{specenr}

The following forgetful 2-functors are equivalences:

\begin{enumerate}
\item $${\barwedge \Cat_{\mathrm{lqst}}} \to {\wedge \Cat_{\mathrm{lqst}}}, $$
\item $$\Cat_{\mathrm{oqst}}\barwedge \to {\Cat_{\mathrm{oqst}}}\wedge, $$	
\item $${\barwedge \Cat_{\mathrm{lqst}} \wedge} \to {{\wedge \Cat_{\mathrm{lqst}} \wedge}}, $$
\item $$\wedge \Cat_{\mathrm{oqst}}\barwedge \to \wedge \Cat_{\mathrm{oqst}}\wedge, $$
\item $$ {\barwedge \Cat_{\mathrm{qst}}\barwedge}\to {{\wedge \Cat_{\mathrm{qst}} \wedge}}.$$

\end{enumerate}

\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
(1): The forgetful functor of (1) is conservative. So it suffices to construct a fully faithful left adjoint.
Let $\mC$ be a small lax quasi-stable left Gray-category and $\mD$ a small reduced spectral left Gray-category. %that admits %cosuspensions and coendomorphisms.
We prove that the induced functor $\rho:  \barwedge\Lax\Exc(\bar{\mC}, \mD) \to \wedge\Lax\Exc(\mC, \mD) $ is an equivalence. The spectral left Yoneda-embedding \cite[Notation 5.36., Corollary 5.14., Lemma 2.55.]{heine2024bienriched} is a coendomorphisms preserving spectral left Gray-embedding $\mD \hookrightarrow \mE$ into a presentable spectral left Gray-category. % which is lax stable by \cref{specstab}.
Thus $\rho$ is the pullback of the similarly defined functor for $\mE,$ which we prove to be an equivalence.
%So we can assume that $\mD$ is a presentable spectral left Gray-category.
There is a commutative square 
$$\begin{xy}
\xymatrix{
\barwedge\L\Fun({\Fun\wedge}(\bar{\mC}^\circ, \Sp), \mE) \ar[d] \ar[r]
&  \wedge\L\Fun({\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*), \mE) \ar[d]
\\ 
\barwedge\Lax\Exc(\bar{\mC}, \mE) \ar[r]  & \wedge\Lax\Exc(\mC, \mE) .
}
\end{xy}$$	
The left vertical functor is an equivalence by the universal property of enriched presheaves \cite[Theorem 5.49.]{heine2024bienriched} and because $\barwedge\Lax\Exc(\bar{\mC}, \mE) = \barwedge\Fun(\bar{\mC}, \mE)$ by \cref{exactos}.
The right vertical functor is an equivalence by \cref{laxoplax} and \cref{unistab}. 
So it remains to see that the top functor is an equivalence.
%This functor factors as $$\wedge\L\Fun({\Fun\wedge}(\bar{\mC}^\op, \Sp), \mE) \to \wedge\L\Fun({\Fun\wedge}(\bar{\mC}^\op, \Sp), \mE) \to \wedge\L\Fun({\Lax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\op, \infty\Cat_*), \mE), $$where the first functor is the forgetful functor that is an equivalence by Corollary ....By the universal property of enriched Yoneda-embedding 
This is equivalent to say that the spectral left Gray-embedding $ \bar{\mC} \subset {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*)$
induces an equivalence $\theta: {\Fun\barwedge}(\bar{\mC}^\circ, \Sp) \to {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*)$ of spectral left Gray-categories.
By \cite[Theorem 5.22.]{heine2024bienriched} and \cref{excloci} the left Gray-category $ {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*)$ is generated under small colimits by left tensors of representables. Hence also the canonical refinement to a spectral left Gray-category is generated under small colimits by left tensors of representables.
\cite[Corollary 4.54.]{heine2024bienriched} guarantees that $\theta$ is an equivalence if for every $X \in \mC$ the spectral left Gray-functor
$\gamma:  {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*) \to \Sp$ corepresented by $X$ preserves small colimits and left tensors. By \cref{spgen} the reduced Gray-category $\Sp$ is generated under small colimits and left tensors by coendomorphisms of the sphere spectrum. 
Since source and target of $\gamma$ are lax stable and presentable and $\gamma$ preserves coendomorphisms, $\gamma$ preserves small colimits and left tensors if the underlying reduced left Gray-functor $\beta$ of $\gamma$ preserves small colimits and left tensors.
Lax stability of the source of $\beta$ implies that $\beta$ is lax excisive and for every $n \geq 0$ the $n$-th factor of $\beta$ denoted by $\beta_n: {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*) \to \infty\Cat_*$  is corepresented as a reduced left Gray-functor by $\Omega'^n(\L\Mor_\mC(-,X))$. The structure equivalence $$\L\Mor_{  {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*) }(\Omega'^n(\L\Mor_\mC(-,X)),-)  \to $$$$ \Omega'\L\Mor_{  {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*) }(\Omega'^{n+1}(\L\Mor_\mC(-,X)),-) $$
corresponds by the enriched Yoneda-lemma to the object of $$  \Omega'\L\Mor_{  {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*) }(\Omega'^{n+1}(\L\Mor_\mC(-,X)),\Omega'^n(\L\Mor_\mC(-,X))) \simeq$$$$ \L\Mor_{\mC}(\Omega'^{n+1}(\L\Mor_\mC(-,X)),\Omega'^{n+1}(\L\Mor_\mC(-,X))), $$ which is the identity.
By the enriched Yoneda-lemma $\beta_n$ evaluates at $\Omega'^n(X)$
and identifies with the reduced left Gray-functor $nu_X:  {\Oplax\Exc\wedge}(\mC^\circ, \infty\Cat_*) \to \Sp $ of \cref{forgeto}, which by \cref{locpre2} preserves small colimits and left tensors. The proof (2) is similar to the one of (1).

