We now consider the probability $P_{\square}(l,t;p)$ of finding an empty region
of size $l \times t$ within the dynamics, see Fig.~\ref{fig:Fig3}(a) for a
precise definition.  In particular, we want to study how the probability
scales for large sizes. We assume $l$ and $t$ to be integer numbers for
simplicity, however, generalisations to semi-integers follow naturally, and do
not change the scaling. In~\cite{klobas2023exact}, the above probability has
been computed in the deterministic limit when $p=1$ and gives
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:Psquaredet}
