\begin{equation}
    E[Y_i(T_i + 1) - Y_i(T_i)] = \sum_{t=0}^\infty (f(t + 1) - f(t)) p(t),
\end{equation}
where $p$ is the mass function of $T_i$.  However, because the RORR plim is a weighted average of derivatives, we focus on the ACD in Table~\ref{tab:rorr_acd} and propose a consistent estimator of the AIE in Section~\ref{sec:aipw}.  As Table~\ref{tab:rorr_acd} shows, the RORR plim is negatively biased for the ACD.  This is due to the fact that it places more weight on the derivative of the dose-response curve at larger values of the treatment.  In the following section, we propose a consistent estimator for the AIE with integer-valued treatments and the ACD with continuous treatments.

