	\section{Numerical Analysis}\label{sec:NA}
	In this section, we provide several numerical examples to illustrate the impacts of competitive components on the equilibrium feedback strategy.

	\begin{figure}[h!]
		\centering
		\includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{phi.eps}  % 引入 EPS 文件
		\caption{\small{The feedback equilibrium  feedback  strategy of agent with respect to  competitive parameter \(\phi_i\)}}
		\label{fig:phi}
	\end{figure}	



In Figure \ref{fig:phi}, we address the effect of the competitive parameter \(\phi_i\) on  the feedback strategy \(\widehat{\pi}_i\) with competition concerns and the feedback strategy \(\tilde{\pi}_i\) without competition concerns for the \(i\)-th agent. We sample $1000$ times from the uniform distribution \( U([0.1,1] \times [0.1,0.2] \times [0.01,0.05]^2 \times [1,10] \times [0,1] \times [0,1]) \) to generate the type vector \( (x_i, b_i, \xi_i, \sigma_i, \gamma_i, \mu_{i1}, \mu_{i2})_{i = 1}^{1000} \), and sample 999 times from the uniform distribution \( U([0,1]) \) to generate a sample sequence \( \{\phi_j\}_{j = 1, j \neq i}^{1000} \). For \( i = 500 \), we set the sample values \( (x_{500}, b_{500}, \xi_{500}, \sigma_{500}, \gamma_{500}, \mu_{500,1}, \mu_{500,2})=(0.35, 0.16, 0.03, 0.01, 4.24, 0.16, 0.98) \), which are obtained from the 500th sample of the uniform distribution \( U([0.1,1] \times [0.1,0.2] \times [0.01,0.05]^2 \times [1,10] \times [0,1] \times [0,1]) \). And we set \(r=0.05\) and \(\lambda=0.04\). Figure \ref{fig:phi} shows that the MFE strategy \(\widehat{\pi}_i\) increases with the competitive parameter $\phi_i$. This is intuitively reasonable because a higher competition parameter signifies more intense competition among market agents, prompting the
$i$-th agent to increase investments in risky assets to maximize the mean-variance objective. This finding is consistent with the results of \citet{lacker2019mean} and \citet{bo2024mean} when the agents follow CARA preferences. However, in a non-competitive investment market, the feedback strategy \(\tilde{\pi}_{i}\) of the \(i\)-th(\(i=500\)) agent remains constant, which is analogous to the ``lying flat'' phenomenon mentioned in \citet{bo2024mean}.


	\begin{figure}[h!]
		\centering
		\includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{gamma.eps}  % 引入 EPS 文件
		\caption{\small{The feedback equilibrium  feedback  strategy of agent with respect to risk aversion  parameter \(\gamma_i\)}}
		\label{fig:gamma}
	\end{figure}	



	In Figure \ref{fig:gamma}, we illustrate the influence of the risk aversion parameter \(\gamma_i\) on the feedback strategy \(\widehat{\pi}_i\) considering competition and the feedback strategy \(\tilde{\pi}_i\) without competition. We sample 1000 times from the uniform distribution \(U([0.1,1]\times [0.1,0.2]\times [0.01,0.05]^2\times [0,1]^3)\) to generate the type vector \((x_i, b_i, \xi_i, \sigma_i, \phi_i, \mu_{i1}, \mu_{i2})_{i = 1}^{1000}\), and 999 times from \(U([1,10])\) to generate \(\{\gamma_j\}_{j = 1, j\neq i}^{1000}\). For \(i = 500\), we set \((x_{500}, b_{500}, \xi_{500}, \sigma_{500}, \phi_{500}, \mu_{500,1},\mu_{500,2})=(0.39, 0.14, 0.03, 0.04, 0.25, 0.28, 0.52)\). We also set \(r=0.05\) and \(\lambda=0.04\). Figure \ref{fig:gamma} shows that
	both \(\widehat{\pi}_i\) and \(\tilde{\pi}_i\) decrease as the risk aversion parameter $\gam_i$ increases. When the risk aversion parameter is higher, the \(i\)-th agent becomes more conservative and risk-averse, leading to reduce investments in risky assets. Furthermore, from Figure \ref{fig:gamma}, we observe that as $\gam_i$ increases, the curve of \(\widehat{\pi}_i\) with competition concerns lies above the curve of the optimal strategy \(\tilde{\pi}_i\) without competition. This observation implies that the agents also consider peer competitive factors in their decision-making process, and are more cautious in investment and risk management to maintain competitiveness in the market. Thus, the agents consider both investment risk and market competition in the decision-making process.

	\begin{figure}[h!]
		\centering
		\includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{mu1.eps}
		\caption{The feedback equilibrium  feedback  strategy of agent with respect to parameter \(\mu_{i1}\)}
